NOTICE

This folder contains code adapted from the repository
https://github.com/songwenas12/fjsp-drl (commit d7637b70029be6cb8fe78e450dcb07767876daea),
the implementation of W. Song, X. Chen, Q. Li and Z. Cao, "Flexible Job-Shop
Scheduling via Graph Neural Network and Deep Reinforcement Learning," IEEE
Transactions on Industrial Informatics, 19(2):1600-1610, 2023,
DOI 10.1109/TII.2022.3189725. That code is licensed under the Apache License,
Version 2.0; the license text is kept in LICENSE in this folder.

Changes to the upstream files
  env/fjsp_env.py    one line in next_time(): the boolean-mask assignment
                     aa[d, 0] = 1, which PyTorch 2 rejects, is written as
                     aa[:, 0, :][d] = 1 (same intended effect: mark the released
                     machines idle). Otherwise unchanged; used as the control.
  env/load_data.py   two functions appended: load_time_lags() reads the
                     per-operation lags from the side-car <stem>.meta.json, and
                     matrix_to_lines() writes a (job_length, op_pt) instance in
                     the .fjs line format.

Files added
  env/fjsp_env_lag.py  copy of env/fjsp_env.py extended with post-operation
                       time-lags (lag_mode 'aware' or 'blind'), optional lag
                       features (ope_feat_dim 8), and an optional
                       minimum-processing-time estimate (bound_pt 'min').
  compat.py            stand-ins for gym and pynvml and the removed
                       pandas.ExcelWriter.save, so the upstream files run as is.
  ppvc_hgnn.py, train_ppvc.py, eval_ppvc_hgnn.py, test_hgnn_lag.py,
  tools/run_upstream_test.py
All other files are copied unchanged.
